Corrected — stopped parallel digging. The nginx source read did land before the correction: `ngx_http_keepalive_handler` does NOT stamp `Connection: close`; on timeout it marks idle + re-arms a second-phase timer (only when `keepalive_min_timeout &gt; 0`), or closes. Defaults: `keepalive_timeout 75s`, `keepalive_requests 1000`. The `Keep-Alive:` header is opt-in only (`if (clcf-&gt;keepalive_header)`).

