## 11327-11354 · Designed the Infernix keep-alive fix mechanism table through user corrections
Designed the keep-alive fix mechanism table for infernix-serve through iterative user corrections. Key verifications: (1) the kill IS the release mechanism — worker released when keep_alive returns false, so starvation is bounded at 60 s by construction; (2) HTTP/1.1 cannot send unsolicited Connection: close at idle (no outstanding request to attach it to); (3) cpp-httplib has zero HTTP/2 support (verified vendored source + README); (4) RFC 9112 §9.6 half-close is already implemented upstream (PR #2534, merged 2026-08-09, vendored in our copy) — the "silent kill" narrative was imprecise, the actual symptom is drain-discards (transport-honored, protocol-thrown-away).

