U: "and that's exactly what i wanted since those froggeric and sharp makes output broken in a lot of cases, like you put description of an action inside thinking block so i don't see it unless i'll dig into your reasoning while ninfer template works perfectly"

The user confirmed the rationale: froggeric/Sharp templates carry a hard instruction ("ALL explanation and reasoning MUST be placed strictly inside the &lt;think&gt;&lt;/think&gt; block") that hides action descriptions from the visible stream. The NInfer base says the opposite — "You may provide optional reasoning for your function call in natural language BEFORE the function call" — keeping narration visible. The terseness block is orthogonal (pure system-prompt text, no tool-protocol changes), which is why the splice preserves working behavior and adds only the brevity layer.

User asked whether `terse=false` is just a template-internal conditional — confirmed yes, a jinja variable read at render time; inert on Infernix unless the server forwards unknown kwargs (untested). User loaded the template; I confirmed live: PID 69756, booted 18:17:07, command line carries `--chat-template chat_templates\qwen3_8_flash_next_medium_terse.jinja`.

